q-126340" :question/id #uuid "f565581c-3596-5b33-9191-b3b143b96ba2" :question/math-academy-id "q-126340" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${c}_{21}=-5\\ne 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126340/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126340"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-13759"] :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${a}_{21}=3\\ne 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-13779/selection/06285049f72ef30fee6ef6292e1826eabf19578fd3f3da4353e2d47878d19d9f" :answer/id #uuid "06ae6a9a-903f-5067-b94c-f6e970a0f366" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Other" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13779/selection/737ed29dfe85abe89843c2e0e81c86e7e8aabd9ae79ced44e8547ea03ce61f3c" :answer/id #uuid "ff871c76-2229-5cc9-8790-ec48f62abb92" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/ensure [:answer/valid